# KANBAN-BOARD API

A RESTful backend API for a Kanban-style task management system (similar to Trello or ClickUp).
Supports user authentication, boards, columns, and cards with full CRUD functionality.
Project is built in Node.js and Express, used Prisma with Neon for database.


## NOTES
- Make sure .env is setup properly.
- I set up PORT to be 9000/9001 but it can be changed to any PORT by changing inside .env or server.js.
- All board, column, and card routes require a valid JWT token sent via the Authorization header.
- Users can only access and modify boards, columns, and cards they own.

## Tech Stack
- Node.js
- Express.js
- Prisma
- Prisma Client
- bcryptjs
- dotenv
- nodemon
- jsonwebtoken

## Features
- User authentication with JWT
- Create and manage boards/columns/cards
- Columns within boards
- Cards within columns
- Move cards between columns
- Secure routes with ownership checks
- Board, column, and card positions are automatically updated when creating/deleting/moving.


## API Endpoints

AUTH ROUTES
METHOD       ROUTES                     DESCRIPTION
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST         /auth/register             Registers a user.
POST         /auth/login                Logs in a user.
POST         /auth/logout               Logs out a user. (Client-side logout (JWT token removal))

BOARD ROUTES
METHOD       ROUTES                     DESCRIPTION
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST         /boards/                   Creates a new board.
PATCH        /boards/:boardId           Edit board name.
DELETE       /boards/:boardId           Deletes board. (This will delete all columns/cards associated with board.)

COLUMN ROUTES
METHOD       ROUTES                     DESCRIPTION
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST         /columns/:boardId          Creates a new column on the board.
PATCH        /columns/:columnId         Edit column name.
DELETE       /columns/:columnId         Deletes column. (This will delete all cards associated with column.)

CARD ROUTES
METHOD       ROUTES                     DESCRIPTION
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST         /cards/:columnId           Creates a new card on the column.
PATCH        /cards/:cardId             Edit card title.
DELETE       /cards/:cardId             Deletes card.
PATCH        /cards/:cardId/:columnId   Updates card columnId. (This works when you move one card to another column.)


## Project Setup

- Clone the repository
    git clone https://github.com/danielmiguel02/KANBAN-BOARD.git
    cd KANBAN-BOARD

- Install Dependencies
    npm i

- Environment Variables
    Create a .env file in the root of the project and add the required credentials:
    DATABASE_URL="" // Inside Neon you will be able to grab the url.
    PORT=9000 // Or change it to what you would like to be the PORT.
    NODE_ENV="development"
    JWT_SECRET="" // node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
    JWT_EXPIRES_IN="7d"

- Running the project
    npm run dev

- Authorization
    Authorization: Bearer <your_token_here>


## POST Example

AUTH REGISTER (http://localhost:9000/auth/register)
{
    "name": "Josh",
    "email": "emailtoregister@gmail.com",
    "password": "password123"
}

AUTH LOGIN (http://localhost:9000/auth/login)
{
    "email": "emailtoregister@gmail.com",
    "password": "password123"
}

BOARD CREATE (http://localhost:9000/boards/)
{
    "name": "board name here"
}

BOARD EDIT (http://localhost:9000/boards/:boardId)
{
    "name": "board edited name"
}

COLUMN CREATE (http://localhost:9000/columns/:boardId)
{
    "name": "new column"
}

COLUMN EDIT (http://localhost:9000/columns/:columnId)
{
    "name": "column edited name"
}

CARD CREATE (http://localhost:9000/cards/:columnId)
{
    "title": "new card"
}

CARD EDIT (http://localhost:9000/cards/:cardId)
{
    "title": "card edited title"
}

